Reprise fixes for untrunc 9d86ec9ef2ffed1bf8131abe80742c0574db52b6 (GPL-2.0, see COPYING).

1. avc1/hvc1: the learned frame-size upper bound was also applied to the first slice of a picture.
   A damaged recording with a busier scene than the healthy reference stopped at the first larger frame
   (or split SEI from its IDR slice). The first slice is now only rejected when implausibly large
   (> 8x the largest allowed sample); the bound still guards merging further slices.
2. mp4: a full-size final chunk ending exactly at the end of the data was rejected as having "no future",
   dropping the last audio chunk.

